            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to get lost, then the Persian for a landmark."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: تقاطع",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تقاطع (taqâto') — \"a crossroads, an intersection\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تاکسی در تقاطع دوم به راست پیچید. Tâksi dar taqâto'-e dovvom be râst pichid. The taxi turned right at the second crossroads."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "More formal than chahârrâh."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "taqâto' was borrowed from Arabic taqāṭuʿ, which EtymDB lists; it is usually glossed 'cutting across each other'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
