          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "سه راه (serâh) — \"a T-junction, a three-way junction\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "به سه راه رسیدیم و نمیدانستیم کدام طرف برویم. Be serâh residim va nemidânestim kodâm taraf beravim. We reached the junction and didn't know which way to go."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "se 'three' + râh 'road'. A crossroads is chahârrâh."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "serâh is a native compound of se 'three', usually traced to PIE tréyes, and râh 'road', from Middle Persian rāh (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
