          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "دوراهی (dorâhi) — \"a fork (in the road); a dilemma\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "در دوراهی راه سمت چپ را گرفتیم. Dar dorâhi râh-e samt-e chap râ gereftim. At the fork we took the road on the left."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also figurative: sar-e dorâhi budan — to be at a crossroads in life."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "dorâhi is a native compound of do 'two', which EtymDB traces to PIE dwóh₁, râh 'road', from Middle Persian rāh (EtymDB), and the ending -i."
            }
          ]
        },
